        "person" : "A Union soldier and a Confederate soldier",
        "action" : "hauling the Wall's two black wings apart at the hinge",
        "object" : "a granite joint that strains but holds",
        "notes" : "“Now we are engaged in a great civil war, testing whether that nation, or any nation so conceived and so dedicated, can long endure.” A Union soldier and a Confederate soldier each seize one black wing of the Wall and haul in opposite directions, testing whether the joint at its apex can hold, while the three bronze soldiers nearby watch to see if it endures."
      }
