        "action" : "hanging a golden halo high above the museum's dome",
        "object" : "a halo out of reach of any ladder",
        "notes" : "“The brave men, living and dead, who struggled here, have consecrated it, far above our poor power to add or detract.” Soldiers living and dead climb the museum's dome arm in arm and hang a golden halo above it, so high that no ladder in Washington can reach it to add a thing or take one away."
