        "person" : "General Grant on his bronze horse",
        "action" : "handing a sculptor's chisel down to the living",
        "object" : "a half-finished bronze charge",
        "notes" : "“It is for us the living, rather, to be dedicated here to the unfinished work which they who fought here have thus far so nobly advanced.” Grant leans down from his bronze horse and hands a chisel to the living to finish the charge his soldiers began, as others finished this very memorial after its sculptor died, twenty years into the work and two weeks before it was dedicated."
